          <declname>aCloseApproach</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const Shared&lt; const <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1_hard_body" kindref="compound">HardBody</ref> &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>aHardBody1SPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const Shared&lt; const <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1_hard_body" kindref="compound">HardBody</ref> &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>aHardBody2SPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const bool &amp;</type>
          <declname>scaleObject1Covariance</declname>
          <defval>true</defval>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const bool &amp;</type>
          <declname>scaleObject2Covariance</declname>
          <defval>true</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute the probability of collision analysis of a close approach using a probability of collision algorithm. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The analysis is not applicable to algorithms computing a maximum probability of collision (see <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1_probability_of_collision_algorithm_1a11cb3a2a30f70e8dd5ccecbadde74348" kindref="member">isMaximum()</ref>), as their probability of collision is already an upper bound.</para>
<para>This function computes the probability of collision and locates the maximum probability of collision as it scales the covariance(s): starting from the unscaled covariance(s), a root solver (bracket and solve) locates where the slope of the probability of collision with respect to the (logarithmic) scaling factor changes sign. The probability of collision is assumed to have a single maximum.</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>If the maximum probability of collision is found to the &quot;right&quot; of the probability of collision (i.e. a scaling factor greater than or equal to 1), then the close approach is in the robust region (<ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1_probability_of_collision_algorithm_1ab68a8a2466868fb02312fd951dd0dd34acd8257a80d3498e67b8972607c8377c0" kindref="member">ProbabilityRegion::Robust</ref>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If the maximum probability of collision is found to the &quot;left&quot; of the probability of collision (i.e. a scaling factor less than 1), then the close approach is in the diluted region (<ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1_probability_of_collision_algorithm_1ab68a8a2466868fb02312fd951dd0dd34ad93c90e25e2dd62f57b5983a12e1b0e2" kindref="member">ProbabilityRegion::Diluted</ref>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If the root solver does not converge (e.g. the probability of collision does not change with the covariance scaling, or has no maximum), then the region is unknown (<ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1_probability_of_collision_algorithm_1ab68a8a2466868fb02312fd951dd0dd34a88183b946cc5f0e8c96b2e66e1c74a7e" kindref="member">ProbabilityRegion::Unknown</ref>).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The scaling factors yielding the maximum probability of collision are also returned, both as a covariance scaling factor and as a sigma scaling factor. In the unknown region (<ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1_probability_of_collision_algorithm_1ab68a8a2466868fb02312fd951dd0dd34a88183b946cc5f0e8c96b2e66e1c74a7e" kindref="member">ProbabilityRegion::Unknown</ref>), the maximum probability of collision and its scaling factors are empty.</para>
<para>Raises an Undefined error if the probability of collision algorithm is null, and a RuntimeError if it computes a maximum probability of collision or if neither covariance is to be scaled.</para>
<para>Alfano, Salvatore. (2020). Relating Position Uncertainty to Maximum Conjunction Probability. The Journal of the Astronautical Sciences. 53. 193-205. 10.1007/BF03546350.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aProbabilityOfCollisionAlgorithmSPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A probability of collision algorithm (not computing a maximum probability of collision) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aCloseApproach</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A close approach </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aHardBody1SPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The hard body of Object 1 </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aHardBody2SPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The hard body of Object 2 </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>scaleObject1Covariance</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to scale Object 1 covariance. Defaults to true </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>scaleObject2Covariance</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to scale Object 2 covariance. Defaults to true</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The probability of collision analysis of the close approach </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
